  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"The Storage screen (command $0f, also Change Disk). Draws the screen (script $23ac), sends \"I\" to the drive, reads the directory and shows each file whose name starts with $81 \"PIC \" in the next slot. Then it runs the Storage loop. Returns after a long press off the pad."},
    {"at":18,"placement":"side","text":"Clears the colours of the sprites ($19e1)."},
    {"at":32,"placement":"line","text":"Opens the directory: file name \"$\", secondary address $60, $f3d5 sends the name. storage_free_slot starts at 1."},
    {"at":51,"placement":"side","text":"KERNAL: sends LISTEN, the secondary address and the file name."},
    {"at":62,"placement":"line","text":"Makes the drive talk, then reads the disk name (the text between the first quotes, at most 12 characters) to row 1, column 22 of the screen."},
    {"at":81,"placement":"side","text":"Destination: the screen at row 1, column 22."},
    {"at":91,"placement":"side","text":"FNLEN is a counter here."},
    {"at":115,"placement":"line","text":"Next directory line: skips to its quote, compares the first 5 bytes of the name with pic_name_prefix and puts the 15 bytes of the name in dir_entry_buffer."},
    {"at":130,"placement":"side","text":"$bc counts the 5 bytes of the prefix."},
    {"at":134,"placement":"side","text":"FNADR is the index into pic_name_prefix here."},
    {"at":173,"placement":"side","text":"Slot number of this file."},
    {"at":197,"placement":"line","text":"End of the directory or a read error: $f642 closes the serial file."},
    {"at":197,"placement":"side","text":"KERNAL: closes the serial file."},
    {"at":203,"placement":"line","text":"KERNAL error 5: writes \"Device Not Present\" to drive_message."},
    {"at":213,"placement":"line","text":"KERNAL error 4: shows \"File not found\"."},
    {"at":223,"placement":"line","text":"A = the KERNAL error code of a failed load or save (carry set): 4 and 5 have their own texts, other codes show \"error\"."},
    {"at":241,"placement":"line","text":"No action: clears storage_action and the label sprites of the cursor."},
    {"at":252,"placement":"line","text":"Storage loop: a long press off the pad returns to the caller. A press on a cell runs the cell."},
    {"at":261,"placement":"line","text":"Hit test of the cursor; a press clears the marks and the message, then selects the action of the cell code."},
    {"at":317,"placement":"side","text":"Slot number 1-16."},
    {"at":322,"placement":"side","text":"A slot after the first empty slot becomes the first empty slot."},
    {"at":327,"placement":"line","text":"A slot: the slot number is at most storage_free_slot. Sets the destination to the slot field, then runs storage_action."},
    {"at":352,"placement":"line","text":"Init Disk: asks \"Erase Disk?\"; only \"Y\" continues. Then gets a disk name of 1-12 characters, sends \"N0:name,id\" and checks the drive status."},
    {"at":354,"placement":"side","text":"Empties the keyboard buffer."},
    {"at":384,"placement":"side","text":"The disk name has at most 12 characters."},
    {"at":415,"placement":"line","text":"Save: storage_action = 1 and the cursor label \"save\"."},
    {"at":427,"placement":"line","text":"Get: storage_action = 2 and the cursor label \"get\"."},
    {"at":439,"placement":"line","text":"Name & Save: storage_action = 3 and the cursor label \"name\"."},
    {"at":451,"placement":"line","text":"Saves the picture to the slot. A slot that has a file: sends \"S0:\" and the old name first."},
    {"at":465,"placement":"side","text":"The slot has a file: build the scratch command with the old name."},
    {"at":483,"placement":"line","text":"The first empty slot: clears the name (not after Name & Save) and adds the slot."},
    {"at":498,"placement":"line","text":"Sets the file name from the slot field and saves the picture ($3351)."},
    {"at":509,"placement":"line","text":"Gets the picture of the slot. The first empty slot does nothing."},
    {"at":519,"placement":"line","text":"Shows \"Getting Picture\", sets the file name from the slot field and loads the picture ($33a6)."},
    {"at":537,"placement":"line","text":"The save and load routines jump here when the drive status is not 00 after the open: removes their return address and shows the error."},
    {"at":547,"placement":"line","text":"Shows drive_message on the message line."},
    {"at":564,"placement":"line","text":"Name & Save to the slot: gets a name of 1-8 characters, then saves. A slot that has a file: sends \"S0:\" and the old name first."},
    {"at":616,"placement":"line","text":"Sets the file of a picture: name = the 15 bytes at script_dst (the slot field: $81 \"PIC \", the letter, a space and the name), logical file 5, device 8, secondary address 0."},
    {"at":616,"placement":"side","text":"15 characters: the name in the slot field."},
    {"at":634,"placement":"line","text":"Sends the command \"I\" (init_command) to the drive on channel 15. Also used by the disk protection ($3a85)."},
    {"at":643,"placement":"line","text":"Shows \"Formatting Disk\" and sends the 18 bytes of disk_command (\"N0:name,id\") to the drive."},
    {"at":650,"placement":"line","text":"Sends the 18 bytes of disk_command to the drive on channel 15."},
    {"at":656,"placement":"line","text":"Opens the command channel with the name in A/X/Y, then closes file 15."},
    {"at":664,"placement":"line","text":"Opens file 15 on device 8, secondary address 15, with the name of length A at X/Y (SETNAM, SETLFS, OPEN). Also used by the disk protection ($3a62, $3a78)."},
    {"at":679,"placement":"line","text":"Sets the destination to the field of the slot in hit_code."},
    {"at":681,"placement":"line","text":"Sets the destination (script_dst) to the field of slot A (1-16). Slots 1-8 are the left column, 9-16 the right column. Changes script_condition."},
    {"at":681,"placement":"side","text":"Slots 1-8: script_condition = slot (not zero) means the left column."},
    {"at":709,"placement":"line","text":"Clears the name of the slot field and gets a name of at most 8 characters. Carry set: no characters."},
    {"at":716,"placement":"side","text":"The picture name has at most 8 characters."},
    {"at":721,"placement":"line","text":"Text entry at the destination: at most entry_max_length characters $20-$5a, DEL removes one, RETURN ends. Carry set: no characters. The script code draws the characters and the caret."},
    {"at":731,"placement":"side","text":"DEL."},
    {"at":753,"placement":"side","text":"RETURN."},
    {"at":804,"placement":"line","text":"Reads the status of the drive on channel 15 ($3adf) into drive_message after the text \"Error\". Carry clear: status 00."},
    {"at":815,"placement":"line","text":"Reads bytes from the serial bus up to a zero byte. Z clear: the read ended with a status."},
    {"at":820,"placement":"line","text":"Reads bytes from the serial bus up to a quote. Z clear: the read ended with a status."},
    {"at":834,"placement":"line","text":"Reads a byte from the serial bus (ACPTR) to A. Y = STATUS, Z set when STATUS is 0."},
    {"at":840,"placement":"line","text":"Writes A at the destination (script_put_fill_value) and increments the destination."},
    {"at":849,"placement":"line","text":"Waits for a key: lets the IRQ scan the keyboard, waits for 10 empty GETIN results, then waits for a key and stops the keyboard scan. Returns the key in A."},
    {"at":849,"placement":"side","text":"The IRQ calls SCNKEY while keyboard_scan_enable is not zero."}
  ],
